    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The duchy became the first Protestant state when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-duke-of-prussia">Albert, Duke of Prussia</a>, adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in 1525 and held his lands as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fief">fief</a> of the Polish Crown.</li><li>The duchy was inherited by the Hohenzollern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1618, a personal union known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">Frederick William, the Great Elector</a>, won full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wehlau">Treaty of Wehlau</a> of 1657, the step that allowed the duchy to become a kingdom in 1701.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> himself urged Albert, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a> in 1522 and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> in 1524, to turn the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>'s land into a secular principality, and helped broker the deal.</p></aside>
    </section>

