-year">1569</span><span class="rf-text">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lublin">Lublin</a>, Albert Frederick pays homage to Sigismund II, who enfeoffs <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-ii-hector">Joachim II of Brandenburg</a> and his descendants as co-heirs</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1618</span><span class="rf-text">The duchy passes to the Hohenzollern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1657</span><span class="rf-text">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wehlau">Treaty of Wehlau</a>, John II Casimir Vasa recognises Frederick William's full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the duchy</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1662</span><span class="rf-text">Frederick William enters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a> with his troops and forces the city to swear allegiance to him</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1701</span><span class="rf-text">Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-prussia">Frederick III of Brandenburg</a> becomes King in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, and the duchy is elevated to a kingdom</span></li></ol>
